@startuml the_fixing_screens_and_what_each_is_for
title The fixing screens, the question each answers and who asks it

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Super administrator" as sysadmin
actor "System administrator" as admin
actor "Party operations" as ops
actor "Party front office" as fo

package "Market data" {
  component "Fixings\n(the system view)" as browser
  component "Public rates" as public
  component "Fixing series\none item by its address" as series
}

package "The party" {
  component "Fixings manager" as manager
  component "Control reports" as controls
}

database "Fixing series\nobservations, under the system party" as store
database "Party fixings\nadoption, status, override" as party

sysadmin --> browser : what did the sources state
admin --> public : is each publisher arriving
fo --> manager : key a value before its date
ops --> manager : authorise, override, undo
ops --> controls : did the process miss anything

browser --> store : reads, never writes
public --> store : reads, and asks a supplier for more
series --> store : reads one item
manager --> store : reads the observation
manager --> party : writes the adoption
controls --> party : reads the status

browser ..> series : a row opens
manager ..> series : the observation opens
public ..> series : a publisher's item opens

note bottom of browser
  No authorisation and no act.
  A day nobody stated is shown missing.
end note

note bottom of manager
  The only place a party's
  fixing is decided.
end note

@enduml
